{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794987669,"nonce":"vZMZzgTl7j9s7Kt4bYmWk3LhuEQ=","title":"[GitHub #80] text_area: stale scroll offset when the area grows after an edit (ensure_cursor_visible uses the old height)","message":"Source: https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/issues/80\nReporter: FreeSynergy\nGitHub state at capture: open\nReported: 2026-11-17T00:33:00Z; updated: 2026-11-17T00:33:00Z\nCaptured: 2026-11-18T07:38:25.958Z\n\nStatus: queued from the upstream report. This import does not claim local reproduction, implementation or a fix.\n\nTracking scope and expected outcome\n\nReproduce text_area growth after repeated Enter/edit events. Once the latest viewport fits all visual lines, clamp/reset the stale scroll offset immediately so the first line is visible without another key press. Preserve caret visibility for actual overflow, wrapping and shrinking viewports. The reported repeated -19.6 offset should become 0 after each growth step.\n\nOriginal GitHub report\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen a `text_area` is sized to its content (the app rebuilds it with `.rows(n)` after the line count changes), typing Enter or a character at the end of the text scrolls the area using the *old* viewport height. After the area has grown to fit all lines, the scroll offset stays non-zero, so the top of the text is hidden although everything would fit. The offset is only corrected by the next key press.\n\n## Expected\n\nAfter the area has grown so that all lines fit, the scroll offset is 0 and the first line is visible.\n\n## Actual\n\nIn `text_area/handlers.rs` (lines 285 and 438 on current upstream main) the key handlers call `d.ensure_cursor_visible(line_height, viewport_height)` with the cached `viewport_height`, which still belongs to the previous, smaller area. The cursor is on the new last line, so the area scrolls down by one line. The area is then rebuilt taller, but `scroll_physics.offset_y` keeps the value.\n\nMeasured with the repro below (line height 19.6 px):\n\n| step | lines | offset_y after key | offset_y after area grown to `rows(lines)` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Enter #1 | 2 | -19.6 | -19.6 |\n| Enter #2 | 3 | -19.6 | -19.6 |\n| Enter #3 | 4 | -19.6 | -19.6 |\n| Enter #4 | 5 | -19.6 | -19.6 |\n\nExpected after growth: 0.0 every time. After one more typed character the offset becomes 0 again (the clamp then uses the new height), which is why the first line seems to jump back.\n\n## Minimal repro\n\nIntegration test in `crates/blinc_layout/tests/` (reads `scroll_physics.offset_y`, which is `pub(crate)`, so a one-line test accessor is needed to print it):\n\n```rust\nuse blinc_core::events::event_types;\nuse blinc_layout::event_handler::EventContext;\nuse blinc_layout::renderer::RenderTree;\nuse blinc_layout::widgets::text_area::{text_area, text_area_state};\n\n#[test]\nfn growing_area_keeps_stale_scroll_offset() {\n    blinc_theme::ThemeState::init_default();\n    let state = text_area_state();\n    let build = |rows: usize| {\n        let area = text_area(\u0026state).w(300.0).rows(rows);\n        let mut tree = RenderTree::from_element(\u0026area);\n        tree.compute_layout(400.0, 600.0);\n        (area, tree)\n    };\n    let (mut area, mut tree) = build(1);\n    let root = tree.root().unwrap();\n    let h = |a: \u0026_| blinc_layout::div::ElementBuilder::event_handlers(a).unwrap();\n    h(\u0026area).dispatch(\u0026EventContext::new(event_types::POINTER_DOWN, root)\n        .with_bounds(300.0, 100.0).with_mouse_pos(14.0, 14.0)); // focus\n    for _ in 0..4 {\n        h(\u0026area).dispatch(\u0026EventContext::new(event_types::KEY_DOWN, root).with_key_code(13)); // Enter\n        let rows = state.lock().unwrap().line_count();\n        (area, tree) = build(rows); // content-sized area grows\n        let _ = \u0026tree;\n        // print state.lock().unwrap().scroll_physics.lock().unwrap().offset_y\n        // observed: -19.6 each time, expected 0.0\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Environment\n\nBlinc current upstream main (checked at the commit fetched on 2026-11-17). Linux, headless test, default theme, font size 14 (line height 19.6 px).\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nEither of:\n- re-run `ensure_cursor_visible` (or at least the clamp to `max_scroll`) after layout, when the viewport height is known to have changed (e.g. in `update_scroll_dimensions` / `rows()`), or\n- skip the scroll in the key handlers when the area is configured with `rows(n)` and `n` is at least the number of visual lines, since everything fits.\nResetting a non-zero offset when `content_height \u003c= viewport_height` on a height change would also fix it.\n\nWe are happy to help with a pull request if you tell us which direction you prefer.\n\nAlso tracked in git-bug in our fork FreeSynergy/Blinc (id ff6ddc2).","files":null}]}